1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Select the rectangle tool and draw a plate in the 2D window as the base plate of the bag.

2
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Use the internal line tool to draw an internal line.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Create a sewing line on this line.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Adjust the position of the internal line, because later the top will be sewed into a thread channel.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:41,000
When the plate is relatively large, you can loosen the plate to reach the required size.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Copy the plate and cut it to keep a thread channel plate.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Use the positioning ball to adjust this plate.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Place it on the inner side of the outer plate.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Create a sewing line.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Freeze the outer plate and let the thread channel be sewed together.

11
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:16,000
The size of the plate is relatively small here, so directly reduce the particle diameter to 8 to get the original curve.

12
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
And reduce the conflict thickness to make the plate tight.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Copy a set of plates and turn them over.

14
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Make sure that the holes are facing the front.

15
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Since there is no break point on the side, you can't sew directly using the thread section.

16
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:41,000
If you use free sewing, there is no way to absorb the internal line that has not been made.

17
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
So choose to align the inner line to the inner line of the plate and add points.

18
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Then you can use the sewing line tool to sew.

19
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Unlock the front and open the simulation.

20
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Then unlock all plates and simulate briefly.

21
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Then choose all the plates and place the bag on the ground to adjust later.

22
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
When the particle diameter is relatively high,

23
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,199
When the particle diameter is higher, the outer line of the plate will not be smooth enough

24
00:02:28,599 --> 00:02:31,599
Reducing the particle diameter can get a smoother curve

25
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:48,500
At present, the seam of the bag is not round enough, it looks like there is an obvious fold

26
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:52,500
After hardening, you can see that it is smoother

27
00:02:54,099 --> 00:02:58,900
Due to the hardening, a part of the fold effect will be erased, so choose to change the physical properties

28
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:07,099
By increasing the bending strength, you can make it smoother

29
00:03:11,099 --> 00:03:14,300
Next, we need to make the drawstring effect of the bag

30
00:03:16,599 --> 00:03:18,000
First, add a fixing needle

31
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:18,500
Fixing needle

32
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:20,099
Next, we need to attach the other parts

33
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:33,300
For the effect of tightening the force of the tail end of the plate

34
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,400
This is to add a fixing needle to the top and sides of both sides

35
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,400
and tighten the area.

36
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:57,400
Then delete the fixed pin and return the shrink to 100.

37
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:10,400
As the shrink returns, you can see that there is a fold in the previously fixed area.

38
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:15,400
You can see that there is a fold in the previously fixed area.

39
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:19,399
Then try to make the part of the middle string.

40
00:04:22,399 --> 00:04:27,399
First, freeze all the boards except the top board.

41
00:04:29,399 --> 00:04:33,399
Then use the positioning ball tool to pull the board away from the other boards a little.

42
00:04:33,399 --> 00:04:36,399
Also leave a gap to pass the rope through.

43
00:04:36,399 --> 00:04:39,399
Make a very thin board and use it as a rope.

44
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:45,400
Use the positioning ball tool to quickly position a board near another board.

45
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:48,400
Press the Shift key to place it evenly.

46
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:58,400
Use the positioning ball tool again to place it in the right place.

47
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:16,400
Then, to prevent instability, freeze the rope board and simulate it.

48
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:21,400
To prevent instability, freeze the rope board and simulate it.

49
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:34,400
To reduce the strength of the rope board particles and add a fixing pin to fix both ends.

50
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:38,400
Since all the other boards are in a frozen state,

51
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,400
you can simulate it again.

52
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:42,400
The curse still exists.

53
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:47,400
Then you can adjust the position of the rope through the fixing pin.

54
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,400
This lesson is over.

55
